From 8d288e496421e9dd6bc48cfbdbe64a28467d9842 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:10:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 68/68] temp/libcamera: white balance on nearly grey pixels

New libcamera patches:
0013 collects the pixels that look nearly grey with the current white
balance in separate statistics and bases the AWB on them, so large
coloured areas no longer tint the picture; a greyWeight tuning value
limits how much they count,
0014 adds a minGain tuning value, so red or blue can be attenuated when
they are stronger than green.

Tuning: minGain 0.25 for all five cameras (the colour filter camera sees
near infrared and was stuck with a red cast), and for the front camera
the colour matrices of the stock tuning and greyWeight 0.5 (it mostly
sees light from displays, which made it too cool).
