+From 978072ff9c1ba977e5147fb79a0bd76ceda42368 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Timo <1788603+darknagel@users.noreply.github.com>
+Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:41:42 +0100
+Subject: [PATCH 13/14] software_isp: Base the white balance on nearly grey
+ pixels
+
+The grey world white balance averages the whole frame, so a large coloured
+area (a blue wall, a green lawn) tints the whole picture in the
+complementary colour.
+
+Collect the pixels that look nearly grey with the white balance gains of
+the frame (red and blue within 25 % of green after the gains, unsaturated,
+not too dark) in separate sums of the statistics, and let the AWB use
+them: alone when they make up at least 10 % of the frame, blended with
+the plain grey world from 2 % on, and not at all below. The plain grey
+world keeps the gains moving when they are still far off.
+
+A greyWeight tuning value (0.0 to 1.0, default 1.0) limits how much the
+nearly grey pixels may count, for cameras that mostly see mixed light.
